    """The run log's own rich comment comparison (specs/0024-rich-text.md,
    "Harness runs", --richcomment-sample, P2, with the P1 verification rulings),
    written for M3 part 2 P2 from part 4d P1's cmtcmp.py (the comment sample's
    checks of specs/0022-comments-and-images.md, "Harness runs"): the comment
    the rules give now holds the sample's two runs, and five checks are added
    (two_runs, rich_read, flagged, xml_values, and the rich counts).
    
    Usage: rccmp.py <input archive> <output archive> [--diff <diff.tsv>] [--plant <flag>]
           rccmp.py <input archive> --parts
    
    Reads both archives with zipfile, byte spans and ElementTree, sharing no code
    with the library or the tool. It finds the workbook part through the package
    relationship; W, the first <sheet> in <sheets> order whose relationship type
    is a worksheet's, and its part; whether the workbook's relationship to W is
    of the strict form; M, the largest row number of a <c> in W's sheetData
    elements (0 when there is none), N = M + 1, the sample's cell (N, 1); W's
    rels part and its relationships; W's comments part (the first comments
    relationship's) and W's VML part (the one its legacyDrawing's r:id names);
    the entry names the rules give a created part, xl/comments<n>.xml and
    xl/drawings/vmlDrawing<n>.vml with n the smallest positive integer no input
    entry has (ASCII case folded); the relationship ids, rId one past the largest
    numbered id of W's rels part, the comments relationship first; D, the VML
    part's own idmap number, or the smallest positive integer no VML part of the
    input (an entry named *.vml, case folded) uses as its idmap; and the shape id
    by P1 ruling 1: 1024 * D + K, K one more than the larger of the kept shape
    count and the largest n - 1024 * D over the part's shapes whose id or o:spid
    is _x0000_s<n> with n in D's range. From the input it builds, by the design's
    rules, what the output must hold, and compares:
    
      root_tag       W's root start tag is the input's, or, when the input's has
                     no legacyDrawing and binds no prefix to the relationships
                     namespace, the input's with one bound (r, or the first of r1,
                     r2 and so on it does not declare) in W's form
      rest_same      W with its root start tag and a created legacyDrawing cut out
                     is the input's with its root start tag cut out, byte for byte
      legacy_place   a created legacyDrawing is exactly the element built here
                     (the root's prefix, the relationships prefix, the VML
                     relationship's id), ending where the first root child that
                     follows it in schema order starts, or at the root's end tag
                     (this program's own copy of the worksheet table); a kept one
                     is the input's, byte for byte, the only one
      root_order     the output's main root children's names are the input's with
                     legacyDrawing inserted there when it was created
      rels_bytes     W's rels part is the input's with the created parts'
                     relationships (comments, then VML) in W's form with the
                     relative targets before its end tag, or created in the
                     package's own rels form, or the input's when none is created
      types_bytes    the content types part is the input's with one Override per
                     created part (comments, then VML) before its end tag
      comments_bytes the comments part is exactly the bytes "Comments: the parts"
                     gives when created; when kept, the input's with the author
                     appended before authors' end tag unless a kept author's text
                     is the sample's, and the comment appended before
                     commentList's end tag, each with its container's prefix
      vml_bytes      the VML part is exactly the bytes "Comments: the parts" gives
                     with D and the shape id when created; when kept, the input's
                     bytes up to the root's end tag, the shapetype _x0000_t202 when
                     the input has none and the note shape, each with the root's
                     prefixes, then the rest
      comments_read  read with ElementTree, the output's comments part holds one
                     comment more, the last with the sample's ref, authorId and
                     flattened text, "emend: rich comment"
      two_runs       read with ElementTree, the last comment's text element holds
                     exactly two main r children and nothing else: the first an
                     rPr holding exactly one child, an empty main b with no
                     attribute, then a main t "emend:" with no attribute; the
                     second no rPr, one main t " rich comment" whose only
                     attribute is xml:space="preserve"
      rich_read      the output's comments of runs (a comment whose text holds a
                     main r child, and some run or plain t child with text, the
                     crate's read rule after P1 verification ruling 4) are the
                     input's plus one, the last comment among them with 2 runs
      shapes_read    read with ElementTree, the output's VML part holds one note
                     shape more, the last with the shape id, Row N - 1 and
                     Column 0
      xml_values     with --diff, the runner's diff.<label>.tsv for the pair: its
                     xml "values" rows are exactly the changed entries' the rules
                     give (W when legacyDrawing is created, W's rels part when
                     kept and changed, the content types when changed, the
                     comments part and the VML part when kept: xlsx-diff
                     compares a .vml entry as XML too), each with in_only 0 and
                     out_only
                     the number of values (attributes other than namespace
                     bindings, and text nodes not XML whitespace only, xlsx-diff's
                     definition) in what the rules append to that part, counted by
                     expat over the appended bytes (P1 verification ruling 6: the
                     out_only expectation is derived); without --diff, no
      flagged        with --diff, every entry row of the diff's entries for the
                     pair that the rules change carries the flag descriptor exactly
                     when the input's local header sets general purpose bit 3 (a
                     data descriptor, which the layer keeps, recording the new
                     sizes), and no other row is flagged (P1 verification ruling
                     6: the flagged expectation is derived); without --diff, no
    
    It prints ONE line of counts and yes/no flags and no text, reference, sheet
    name or part name. --parts prints W's part name, its rels part's name, the
    comments entry and the VML entry the output will hold, and 1 or 0 for whether
    the input has W's rels part, W's legacyDrawing and W's comments
    relationship, then, for W, its rels part, the comments entry, the VML entry
    and the content types, 1, 0 or - for whether the input's entry of that name
    sets general purpose bit 3 (- when the input has no such entry), one per
    line, for the log to compare with the runner's rows without printing them. --plant <flag> changes the output as read so that the
    named flag turns to no; the line then says planted=yes, or planted=no when
    the pair gives the plant nothing to change.
    """
    import posixpath
    import re
    import sys
    import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
    import zipfile
    from xml.parsers import expat
    
    MAIN = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/spreadsheetml/main")
    RELS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/relationships"
    ATTR = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/officeDocument/relationships")
    V = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:vml"
    O = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office"
    X = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:excel"
    COMMENTS_TYPE = b"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.comments+xml"
    VML_TYPE = b"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.vmlDrawing"
    
    # ECMA-376 Part 1, 18.3.1.99, the worksheet root's children in order: this
    # program's own copy (specs/0018, "Creating an element"), not the crate's.
    TABLE = (
        "sheetPr dimension sheetViews sheetFormatPr cols sheetData sheetCalcPr "
        "sheetProtection protectedRanges scenarios autoFilter sortState "
        "dataConsolidate customSheetViews mergeCells phoneticPr "
        "conditionalFormatting dataValidations hyperlinks printOptions pageMargins "
        "pageSetup headerFooter rowBreaks colBreaks customProperties cellWatches "
        "ignoredErrors smartTags drawing legacyDrawing legacyDrawingHF drawingHF "
        "picture oleObjects controls webPublishItems tableParts extLst").split()
    assert len(TABLE) == 39
    
    FLAGS = ("root_tag", "rest_same", "legacy_place", "root_order", "rels_bytes", "types_bytes",
             "comments_bytes", "vml_bytes", "comments_read", "two_runs", "rich_read", "shapes_read",
             "xml_values", "flagged")
    
    COMMENT = b"<!-- planted -->"
    LD = "legacyDrawing"
    # The sample's constants (tools/emend-copy, --richcomment-sample): the
    # author, the two runs' texts, the first bold, and the flattened text.
    AUTHOR = b"emend"
    RUN1 = b"emend:"
    RUN2 = b" rich comment"
    TEXT = RUN1 + RUN2
    XML_NS = "http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
    DECL = b'<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>\n'
    
    
    def local(tag):
        if tag.startswith("{"):
            ns, _, name = tag[1:].partition("}")
            return ns, name
        return "", tag
    
    
    def rels_name(part):
        d, base = posixpath.split(part)
        return posixpath.join(d, "_rels", base + ".rels") if base else "_rels/.rels"
    
    
    def rels_of(z, part):
        """(Id, Type, resolved target or None) of a part's rels."""
        name = rels_name(part)
        if name not in z.namelist():
            return []
        out = []
        for el in ET.fromstring(z.read(name)).iter("{%s}Relationship" % RELS):
            external = el.get("TargetMode") == "External"
            target = el.get("Target", "")
            resolved = None if external else (
                target[1:] if target.startswith("/")
                else posixpath.normpath(posixpath.join(posixpath.dirname(part), target)))
            out.append((el.get("Id"), el.get("Type", ""), resolved))
        return out
    
    
    def workbook_of(z):
        office = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, "") if ty.endswith("/officeDocument")]
        return office[0] if len(office) == 1 else None
    
    
    def sheets_of(z, workbook):
        """(part, relationship type) of every <sheet>, in <sheets> order."""
        by_id = {i: (ty, t) for (i, ty, t) in rels_of(z, workbook)}
        out = []
        for el in ET.fromstring(z.read(workbook)).iter():
            ns, name = local(el.tag)
            if ns in MAIN and name == "sheet":
                rid = next((el.get("{%s}id" % a) for a in ATTR if el.get("{%s}id" % a)), None)
                ty, target = by_id.get(rid, ("", None))
                out.append((target, ty))
        return out
    
    
    def pick_w(z, workbook):
        """(W's part, whether its relationship is strict), or (None, False)."""
        for (target, ty) in sheets_of(z, workbook):
            if ty in (ATTR[0] + "/worksheet", ATTR[1] + "/worksheet"):
                return target, ty.startswith(ATTR[1])
        return None, False
    
    
    TOKEN = re.compile(rb"<!--.*?-->|<!\[CDATA\[.*?\]\]>|<[!?][^>]*>|<(/?)[^>]*?(/?)>", re.S)
    
    
    def top_level(data):
        """One (start, end) span per top-level element of some bytes."""
        spans = []
        depth = 0
        at = 0
        for m in TOKEN.finditer(data):
            tok = m.group(0)
            if tok.startswith(b"<!") or tok.startswith(b"<?"):
                continue
            if m.group(1):
                depth -= 1
                if depth == 0:
                    spans.append((at, m.end()))
            elif m.group(2):
                if depth == 0:
                    spans.append((m.start(), m.end()))
            else:
                if depth == 0:
                    at = m.start()
                depth += 1
        return spans
    
    
    def qname(raw):
        return re.match(rb"<([^\s/>]+)", raw).group(1)
    
    
    def split_name(q):
        p, _, n = q.rpartition(b":")
        return (p + b":" if p else b""), n.decode()
    
    
    def start_tag(raw):
        return raw[:raw.find(b">") + 1]
    
    
    def opened(tag):
        slash = tag.rfind(b"/")
        return tag[:slash] + tag[slash + 1:]
    
    
    ATTR_RE = rb'(?<=[\s])%s\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')'
    
    
    def attr_value(tag, name):
        m = re.search(ATTR_RE % re.escape(name), tag)
        return m.group(1)[1:-1] if m else None
    
    
    def with_attr(tag, name, value):
        m = re.search(ATTR_RE % re.escape(name), tag)
        if m:
            q = m.start(1)
            return tag[:q + 1] + value + tag[m.end(1) - 1:]
        last = None
        for last in re.finditer(rb'\s[^\s=/>]+\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')', tag):
            pass
        at = last.end() if last else len(re.match(rb"<[^\s/>]+", tag).group(0))
        return tag[:at] + b" " + name + b'="' + value + b'"' + tag[at:]
    
    
    def root_span(data):
        """(start of the root's start tag, end of it, start of the root's
        content, end of it, the root's prefix)."""
        m = re.search(rb"<([^\s/>?!]+)", data)
        close = data.find(b">", m.start())
        q = m.group(1)
        if data[close - 1:close] == b"/":
            return m.start(), close + 1, close + 1, close + 1, split_name(q)[0]
        return m.start(), close + 1, close + 1, data.rfind(b"</"), split_name(q)[0]
    
    
    def children(data, a, b, rp, root_ns):
        """[(start, end, main local name or None)] of the root's children."""
        out = []
        for (x, y) in top_level(data[a:b]):
            raw = data[a + x:a + y]
            p, n = split_name(qname(raw))
            tag = start_tag(raw)
            decl = rb'\sxmlns:' + re.escape(p[:-1]) if p else rb"\sxmlns"
            own = re.search(decl + rb'\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')', tag)
            if own:
                main = own.group(1)[1:-1].decode() in MAIN
            else:
                main = p == rp and root_ns in MAIN
            out.append((a + x, a + y, n if main else None))
        return out
    
    
    def cut(data, spans):
        parts, at = [], 0
        for (x, y) in sorted(spans):
            parts.append(data[at:x])
            at = y
        parts.append(data[at:])
        return b"".join(parts)
    
    
    def rels_prefix_of(tag):
        """The prefix a start tag binds to the relationships namespace, either
        form, or None."""
        for m in re.finditer(rb'\sxmlns:([^\s=/>]+)\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')', tag):
            if m.group(2)[1:-1].decode() in ATTR:
                return m.group(1)
        return None
    
    
    def prefix_for(tag, uri):
        """The prefix a start tag binds to `uri`, or None."""
        for m in re.finditer(rb'\sxmlns:([^\s=/>]+)\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')', tag):
            if m.group(2)[1:-1].decode() == uri:
                return m.group(1)
        return None
    
    
    def m_of(data):
        """The largest row number of a <c> in every main sheetData root child."""
        m = 0
        for sd in ET.fromstring(data):
            ns, name = local(sd.tag)
            if ns not in MAIN or name != "sheetData":
                continue
            for row in sd:
                for c in row:
                    cns, cname = local(c.tag)
                    if cns in MAIN and cname == "c":
                        got = re.match(r"^\$?[A-Z]+\$?([0-9]+)$", c.get("r", ""))
                        if got:
                            m = max(m, int(got.group(1)))
        return m
    
    
    def relative(src, dst):
        s = src.split("/")[:-1]
        d = dst.split("/")
        common = 0
        while common < len(s) and common < len(d) - 1 and s[common] == d[common]:
            common += 1
        return "../" * (len(s) - common) + "/".join(d[common:])
    
    
    def before_end(data, element):
        """The bytes with element inserted before the root's end tag, the root
        opened up first when it is empty."""
        ts, te, a, b, _ = root_span(data)
        tag = data[ts:te]
        if tag.endswith(b"/>"):
            return data[:ts] + opened(tag) + element + b"</" + qname(tag) + b">" + data[te:]
        return data[:b] + element + data[b:]
    
    
    def package_prefix(z):
        """The bytes a created rels part begins with: the package's own
        _rels/.rels up to its root start tag."""
        data = z.read("_rels/.rels")
        return data[:root_span(data)[0]]
    
    
    def idmap_of(data):
        """The first number of a VML part's o:shapelayout/o:idmap data, or None."""
        try:
            root = ET.fromstring(data)
        except ET.ParseError:
            return None
        for layout in root:
            if layout.tag == "{%s}shapelayout" % O:
                for idmap in layout:
                    if idmap.tag == "{%s}idmap" % O:
                        first = idmap.get("data", "").split(",")[0].strip()
                        return int(first) if first.isdigit() else None
        return None
    
    
    def note_shapes(data):
        """The root's v:shape children whose x:ClientData is of ObjectType Note."""
        out = []
        for shape in ET.fromstring(data):
            if shape.tag != "{%s}shape" % V:
                continue
            for cd in shape.iter("{%s}ClientData" % X):
                if cd.get("ObjectType") == "Note":
                    out.append(shape)
                    break
        return out
    
    
    def comment_list(data):
        """The comments of a comments part's commentList, and its authors' texts."""
        root = ET.fromstring(data)
        comments, authors = [], []
        for el in root:
            ns, name = local(el.tag)
            if ns in MAIN and name == "commentList":
                comments = [c for c in el if local(c.tag)[1] == "comment"]
            if ns in MAIN and name == "authors":
                authors = ["".join(a.itertext()) for a in el if local(a.tag)[1] == "author"]
        return comments, authors
    
    
    def a1(col, row):
        s = ""
        while col:
            col, r = divmod(col - 1, 26)
            s = chr(65 + r) + s
        return "%s%d" % (s, row)
    
    
    def comment_el(p, ref, aid):
        """The comment the rules give: the text element holding the sample's two
        runs, the first with <rPr><b/></rPr>, each <t> with xml:space only when
        its text begins or ends with whitespace (the second)."""
        runs = (b"<" + p + b"r><" + p + b"rPr><" + p + b"b/></" + p + b"rPr><" + p + b"t>" + RUN1
                + b"</" + p + b"t></" + p + b"r><" + p + b"r><" + p + b't xml:space="preserve">' + RUN2
                + b"</" + p + b"t></" + p + b"r>")
        return (b"<" + p + b'comment ref="' + ref + b'" authorId="' + str(aid).encode() + b'"><' + p
                + b"text>" + runs + b"</" + p + b"text></" + p + b"comment>")
    
    
    def is_main(tag, name):
        ns, n = local(tag)
        return ns in MAIN and n == name
    
    
    def run_text(r):
        """A run's text: its main t descendants' texts, concatenated."""
        return "".join("".join(t.itertext()) for t in r.iter() if is_main(t.tag, "t"))
    
    
    def text_el(comment):
        return next((c for c in comment if is_main(c.tag, "text")), None)
    
    
    def is_rich(comment):
        """The crate's read rule after P1 verification ruling 4: the text element
        holds a main r child, and some run, or some plain t child, has text."""
        te = text_el(comment)
        if te is None:
            return False
        runs = [c for c in te if is_main(c.tag, "r")]
        if not runs:
            return False
        plain = ["".join(c.itertext()) for c in te if is_main(c.tag, "t")]
        return any(run_text(r) for r in runs) or any(plain)
    
    
    def rich_runs(comment):
        """The runs the read keeps: main r children of the text element with
        text."""
        te = text_el(comment)
        return [c for c in te if is_main(c.tag, "r") and run_text(c)] if te is not None else []
    
    
    def two_runs_ok(comment):
        te = text_el(comment)
        if te is None or len(te) != 2 or (te.text or "").strip():
            return False
        r1, r2 = list(te)
        if not (is_main(r1.tag, "r") and is_main(r2.tag, "r")) or r1.attrib or r2.attrib:
            return False
        if len(r1) != 2 or len(r2) != 1:
            return False
        rpr, t1 = list(r1)
        if not is_main(rpr.tag, "rPr") or rpr.attrib or len(rpr) != 1:
            return False
        b = rpr[0]
        if not is_main(b.tag, "b") or b.attrib or len(b) or (b.text or ""):
            return False
        t2 = r2[0]
        if not (is_main(t1.tag, "t") and is_main(t2.tag, "t")) or len(t1) or len(t2):
            return False
        return (t1.attrib == {} and (t1.text or "") == RUN1.decode()
                and t2.attrib == {"{%s}space" % XML_NS: "preserve"} and (t2.text or "") == RUN2.decode())
    
    
    def values_in(fragment):
        """xlsx-diff's values in some bytes holding elements: attributes other
        than namespace bindings, and text nodes not XML whitespace only, counted
        by expat with no namespace processing over the bytes wrapped in one
        element."""
        count = {"n": 0}
        text = []
    
        def flush():
            if "".join(text).strip(" \t\n\r"):
                count["n"] += 1
            del text[:]
    
        def start(name, attrs):
            flush()
            count["n"] += sum(1 for a in attrs if a != "xmlns" and not a.startswith("xmlns:"))
    
        def end(name):
            flush()
    
        p = expat.ParserCreate()
        p.StartElementHandler = start
        p.EndElementHandler = end
        p.CharacterDataHandler = text.append
        p.Parse(b"<wrap>" + fragment + b"</wrap>", True)
        return count["n"]
    
    
    def bit3(zin, name):
        """1 or 0 for whether the input's entry sets general purpose bit 3, - when
        there is no such entry."""
        try:
            return "1" if zin.getinfo(name).flag_bits & 0x08 else "0"
        except KeyError:
            return "-"
    
    
    def shapetype(v, o):
        return (b"<" + v + b'shapetype id="_x0000_t202" coordsize="21600,21600" ' + o
                + b'spt="202" path="m,l,21600r21600,l21600,xe"><' + v + b'stroke joinstyle="miter"/><'
                + v + b'path gradientshapeok="t" ' + o + b'connecttype="rect"/></' + v + b"shapetype>")
    
    
    def note(v, o, x, number, k, row, col):
        top = row - 1 if row > 0 else row
        anchor = ("%d, 15, %d, 2, %d, 15, %d, 2" % (col + 1, top, col + 3, top + 4)).encode()
        return (b"<" + v + b'shape id="_x0000_s' + str(number).encode() + b'" type="#_x0000_t202" '
                b'style="position:absolute;margin-left:59.25pt;margin-top:1.5pt;width:108pt;'
                b'height:59.25pt;z-index:' + str(k).encode() + b';visibility:hidden" fillcolor="#ffffe1" '
                + o + b'insetmode="auto"><' + v + b'fill color2="#ffffe1"/><' + v
                + b'shadow on="t" color="black" obscured="t"/><' + v + b"path " + o
                + b'connecttype="none"/><' + v + b'textbox style="mso-direction-alt:auto">'
                b'<div style="text-align:left"/></' + v + b"textbox><" + x
                + b'ClientData ObjectType="Note"><' + x + b"MoveWithCells/><" + x + b"SizeWithCells/><"
                + x + b"Anchor>" + anchor + b"</" + x + b"Anchor><" + x + b"AutoFill>False</" + x
                + b"AutoFill><" + x + b"Row>" + str(row).encode() + b"</" + x + b"Row><" + x
                + b"Column>" + str(col).encode() + b"</" + x + b"Column></" + x + b"ClientData></" + v
                + b"shape>")
    
    
    def info(zin):
        """What the input gives: a dict, or an error string."""
        wb = workbook_of(zin)
        if wb is None or wb not in zin.namelist():
            return "error=no-workbook"
        part, strict = pick_w(zin, wb)
        if part is None or part not in zin.namelist():
            return "error=no-worksheet"
        names = zin.namelist()
        folded = {nm.lower() for nm in names}
        win = zin.read(part)
        root_ns = local(ET.fromstring(win).tag)[0]
        w_rels = rels_of(zin, part)
        kinds = lambda end: (ATTR[0] + end, ATTR[1] + end)
        cin = next((t for (_, ty, t) in w_rels if ty in kinds("/comments") and t is not None), None)
        ld_id = None
        for el in ET.fromstring(win):
            ns, name = local(el.tag)
            if ns in MAIN and name == LD:
                ld_id = next((el.get("{%s}id" % a) for a in ATTR if el.get("{%s}id" % a)), None)
        vin = next((t for (i, ty, t) in w_rels if i == ld_id and ty in kinds("/vmlDrawing")), None) if ld_id else None
        n = 1
        while ("xl/comments%d.xml" % n) in folded:
            n += 1
        centry = cin if cin else "xl/comments%d.xml" % n
        n = 1
        while ("xl/drawings/vmldrawing%d.vml" % n) in folded:
            n += 1
        ventry = vin if vin else "xl/drawings/vmlDrawing%d.vml" % n
        return {"part": part, "strict": strict, "names": names, "win": win, "root_ns": root_ns,
                "w_rels": w_rels, "cin": cin, "vin": vin, "ld": ld_id is not None, "centry": centry,
                "ventry": ventry, "wrels": rels_name(part)}
    
    
    def plant(flag, wout, extra, st):
        """(wout, extra) changed so that `flag` turns to no, or None when the
        pair gives the plant nothing to change. `extra` holds the rels, types,
        comments and VML bytes as read."""
        ts, te, a, b, rp = root_span(wout)
        kids = children(wout, a, b, rp, st["root_ns"])
        lds = [(x, y) for (x, y, n) in kids if n == LD]
        sds = [(x, y) for (x, y, n) in kids if n == "sheetData"]
        e = dict(extra)
        if flag == "root_tag":
            return wout[:te - 1] + b' planted="1"' + wout[te - 1:], e
        if flag == "rest_same":
            others = [(x, y) for (x, y, n) in kids if n != LD]
            if not others:
                return None
            return wout[:others[0][0]] + COMMENT + wout[others[0][0]:], e
        if flag == "legacy_place":
            if not lds:
                return None
            x, y = lds[0]
            raw = wout[x:y]
            m = re.search(rb':id\s*=\s*"[^"]*"', raw)
            if not m:
                return None
            return wout[:x] + raw[:m.start()] + b':id="rId0"' + raw[m.end():] + wout[y:], e
        if flag == "root_order":
            if not lds or not sds:
                return None
            (x1, y1), (x2, y2) = sorted([lds[0], sds[0]])
            return wout[:x1] + wout[x2:y2] + wout[y1:x2] + wout[x1:y1] + wout[y2:], e
        if flag in ("rels_bytes", "types_bytes", "comments_bytes", "vml_bytes"):
            key = flag.split("_")[0]
            if e.get(key) is None:
                return None
            e[key] = e[key] + COMMENT
            return wout, e
        if flag == "comments_read":
            data = e.get("comments")
            if data is None:
                return None
            at = data.rfind(b"</")
            lists = [s for s in top_level(data[root_span(data)[2]:at])]
            cl = None
            base = root_span(data)[2]
            for (x, y) in lists:
                if split_name(qname(data[base + x:base + y]))[1] == "commentList":
                    cl = (base + x, base + y)
            if cl is None:
                return None
            end = data.rfind(b"</", cl[0], cl[1])
            p = split_name(qname(data[cl[0]:cl[1]]))[0]
            e["comments"] = data[:end] + b"<" + p + b'comment ref="A1" authorId="0"/>' + data[end:]
            return wout, e
        if flag in ("two_runs", "rich_read"):
            data = e.get("comments")
            if data is None:
                return None
            if flag == "two_runs":
                at = data.rfind(b"<b/>")
                if at < 0:
                    return None
                e["comments"] = data[:at] + data[at + 4:]
                return wout, e
            # The appended comment's second run emptied, which the read drops.
            at = data.rfind(b">" + RUN2 + b"<")
            if at < 0:
                return None
            e["comments"] = data[:at + 1] + data[at + 1 + len(RUN2):]
            return wout, e
        if flag in ("xml_values", "flagged"):
            e["plant_" + flag] = True
            return wout, e
        if flag == "shapes_read":
            data = e.get("vml")
            if data is None:
                return None
            tag = start_tag(data[root_span(data)[0]:])
            v, x = prefix_for(tag, V), prefix_for(tag, X)
            if v is None or x is None:
                return None
            end = data.rfind(b"</")
            extra_shape = (b"<" + v + b":shape><" + x + b':ClientData ObjectType="Note"><' + x + b":Row>0</"
                           + x + b":Row><" + x + b":Column>0</" + x + b":Column></" + x + b":ClientData></"
                           + v + b":shape>")
            e["vml"] = data[:end] + extra_shape + data[end:]
            return wout, e
        raise KeyError(flag)
    
    
    def yn(v):
        return "yes" if v else "no"
    
    
    def e_plant(extra, flag):
        return bool(extra.get("plant_" + flag))
    
    
    def main():
        args = sys.argv[1:]
        zin = zipfile.ZipFile(args[0])
        got = info(zin)
        if isinstance(got, str):
            print(got)
            return
        part, strict, names, win = got["part"], got["strict"], got["names"], got["win"]
        if args[1:] == ["--parts"]:
            print(part)
            print(got["wrels"])
            print(got["centry"])
            print(got["ventry"])
            print(1 if got["wrels"] in names else 0)
            print(1 if got["ld"] else 0)
            print(1 if got["cin"] else 0)
            for nm in (part, got["wrels"], got["centry"], got["ventry"], "[Content_Types].xml"):
                print(bit3(zin, nm))
            return
        zout = zipfile.ZipFile(args[1])
        flag_plant = None
        diff_path = None
        rest = args[2:]
        if rest[:1] == ["--diff"] and len(rest) >= 2:
            diff_path = rest[1]
            rest = rest[2:]
        if len(rest) == 2 and rest[0] == "--plant":
            flag_plant = rest[1]
            if flag_plant not in FLAGS:
                print("error=unknown-plant")
                return
        elif rest:
            print("error=usage")
            return
        wout = zout.read(part)
        out_names = zout.namelist()
        wrels, centry, ventry, root_ns = got["wrels"], got["centry"], got["ventry"], got["root_ns"]
        extra = {
            "rels": zout.read(wrels) if wrels in out_names else None,
            "types": zout.read("[Content_Types].xml"),
            "comments": zout.read(centry) if centry in out_names else None,
            "vml": zout.read(ventry) if ventry in out_names else None,
        }
    
        # What the rules give, from the input.
        n = m_of(win) + 1
        ref = a1(1, n).encode()
        made_c, made_v = got["cin"] is None, not got["ld"]
        numbers = [int(i[3:]) for (i, _, _) in got["w_rels"] if re.match(r"^rId[0-9]+$", i or "")]
        nxt = max(numbers) + 1 if numbers else 1
        form = ATTR[1 if strict else 0].encode()
        rels_add = b""
        over_add = b""
        # What the rules append to each kept part, for the xml_values flag.
        appended = {}
        rid_v = None
        if made_c:
            rels_add += (b'<Relationship Id="rId%d" Type="' % nxt + form + b'/comments" Target="'
                         + relative(part, centry).encode() + b'"/>')
            over_add += b'<Override PartName="/' + centry.encode() + b'" ContentType="' + COMMENTS_TYPE + b'"/>'
            nxt += 1
        if made_v:
            rid_v = b"rId%d" % nxt
            rels_add += (b'<Relationship Id="' + rid_v + b'" Type="' + form + b'/vmlDrawing" Target="'
                         + relative(part, ventry).encode() + b'"/>')
            over_add += b'<Override PartName="/' + ventry.encode() + b'" ContentType="' + VML_TYPE + b'"/>'
        its, ite, ia, ib, rootp = root_span(win)
        tag_in = win[its:ite]
        bound = rels_prefix_of(tag_in)
        if made_v and bound is None:
            k = 0
            while True:
                cand = b"r" if k == 0 else b"r%d" % k
                if attr_value(tag_in, b"xmlns:" + cand) is None:
                    break
                k += 1
            rp_attr = cand
            want_tag = with_attr(tag_in, b"xmlns:" + cand, form)
        else:
            rp_attr = bound
            want_tag = tag_in
        kin = children(win, ia, ib, rootp, root_ns)
        ld_el = None
        if made_v:
            ld_el = b"<" + rootp + b"legacyDrawing " + rp_attr + b':id="' + rid_v + b'"/>'
            later = [x for (x, _, nm) in kin if nm in TABLE and TABLE.index(nm) > TABLE.index(LD)]
            at = later[0] if later else ib
            want_w = win[:its] + want_tag + win[ite:at] + ld_el + win[at:]
            appended[part] = ld_el
        else:
            want_w = win
        # The comments part.
        if got["cin"]:
            cdata = zin.read(got["cin"])
            comments_in, authors_in = comment_list(cdata)
            kept = AUTHOR.decode() in authors_in
            aid = authors_in.index(AUTHOR.decode()) if kept else len(authors_in)
            ca, cb = root_span(cdata)[2], root_span(cdata)[3]
            want_c = cdata
            edits = []
            for (x, y) in top_level(cdata[ca:cb]):
                raw = cdata[ca + x:ca + y]
                p, name = split_name(qname(raw))
                el = None
                if name == "authors" and not kept:
                    el = b"<" + p + b"author>" + AUTHOR + b"</" + p + b"author>"
                if name == "commentList":
                    el = comment_el(p, ref, aid)
                if el is None:
                    continue
                tag = start_tag(raw)
                if tag.endswith(b"/>"):
                    edits.append((ca + x, ca + y, opened(tag) + el + b"</" + qname(raw) + b">"))
                else:
                    end = raw.rfind(b"</")
                    edits.append((ca + x, ca + y, raw[:end] + el + raw[end:]))
            out, at = b"", 0
            for (x, y, new) in sorted(edits):
                out += cdata[at:x] + new
                at = y
            want_c = out + cdata[at:]
            n_comments_in, n_authors_in = len(comments_in), len(authors_in)
            authors_want = n_authors_in + (0 if kept else 1)
            appended[got["cin"]] = ((b"" if kept else b"<author>" + AUTHOR + b"</author>")
                                    + comment_el(b"", ref, aid))
            rich_in = sum(1 for c in comments_in if is_rich(c))
        else:
            aid = 0
            want_c = (DECL + b'<comments xmlns="' + MAIN[0].encode() + b'"><authors><author>' + AUTHOR
                      + b"</author></authors><commentList>" + comment_el(b"", ref, 0)
                      + b"</commentList></comments>")
            n_comments_in, n_authors_in, authors_want = 0, 0, 1
            rich_in = 0
        # The VML part.
        used = set()
        for nm in names:
            if nm.lower().endswith(".vml"):
                d = idmap_of(zin.read(nm))
                if d is not None:
                    used.add(d)
        alloc = 1
        while alloc in used:
            alloc += 1
        row, col = n - 1, 0
        if got["vin"]:
            vdata = zin.read(got["vin"])
            own = idmap_of(vdata)
            d = own if own is not None else alloc
            vroot = ET.fromstring(vdata)
            shapes = [s for s in vroot if s.tag == "{%s}shape" % V]
            low = 1024 * d
            highest = 0
            for s in shapes:
                for key in ("id", "{%s}spid" % O):
                    m = re.match(r"^_x0000_s([0-9]+)$", s.get(key, ""))
                    if m and low < int(m.group(1)) <= low + 1024:
                        highest = max(highest, int(m.group(1)) - low)
            k = max(len(shapes), highest) + 1
            number = low + k
            vtag = start_tag(vdata[root_span(vdata)[0]:])
            pv, po, px = prefix_for(vtag, V), prefix_for(vtag, O), prefix_for(vtag, X)
            has_type = any(s.tag == "{%s}shapetype" % V and s.get("id") == "_x0000_t202" for s in vroot)
            end = vdata.rfind(b"</")
            if None in (pv, po, px):
                want_v = None
            else:
                add = b"" if has_type else shapetype(pv + b":", po + b":")
                add += note(pv + b":", po + b":", px + b":", number, k, row, col)
                want_v = vdata[:end] + add + vdata[end:]
                appended[got["vin"]] = add
            shapes_in = len(note_shapes(vdata))
        else:
            d, k = alloc, 1
            number = 1024 * d + 1
            want_v = (b'<xml xmlns:v="' + V.encode() + b'" xmlns:o="' + O.encode() + b'" xmlns:x="'
                      + X.encode() + b'"><o:shapelayout v:ext="edit"><o:idmap v:ext="edit" data="'
                      + str(d).encode() + b'"/></o:shapelayout>' + shapetype(b"v:", b"o:")
                      + note(b"v:", b"o:", b"x:", number, 1, row, col) + b"</xml>")
            shapes_in = 0
        if rels_add and wrels in names:
            appended[wrels] = rels_add
        if over_add:
            appended["[Content_Types].xml"] = over_add
        st = {"root_ns": root_ns}
    
        planted = False
        if flag_plant is not None:
            changed = plant(flag_plant, wout, extra, st)
            if changed is not None:
                wout, extra = changed
                planted = True
    
        flags = dict.fromkeys(FLAGS, False)
        ots, ote, oa, ob, orp = root_span(wout)
        kout = children(wout, oa, ob, orp, root_ns)
        ld_out = [(x, y) for (x, y, nm) in kout if nm == LD]
        flags["root_tag"] = wout[ots:ote] == want_tag and wout[:ots] == win[:its]
        cut_in = cut(win, [(its, ite)])
        cut_out = cut(wout, [(ots, ote)] + (ld_out if made_v else []))
        flags["rest_same"] = cut_in == cut_out
        if made_v:
            later = [x for (x, _, nm) in kout if nm in TABLE and TABLE.index(nm) > TABLE.index(LD)]
            end_at = later[0] if later else ob
            flags["legacy_place"] = (len(ld_out) == 1 and wout[ld_out[0][0]:ld_out[0][1]] == ld_el
                                     and ld_out[0][1] == end_at)
        else:
            ld_in = [(x, y) for (x, y, nm) in kin if nm == LD]
            flags["legacy_place"] = (len(ld_out) == 1 and len(ld_in) == 1
                                     and wout[ld_out[0][0]:ld_out[0][1]] == win[ld_in[0][0]:ld_in[0][1]])
        order_in = [nm for (_, _, nm) in kin if nm is not None]
        order_out = [nm for (_, _, nm) in kout if nm is not None]
        if made_v:
            later = [i for (i, nm) in enumerate(order_in) if nm in TABLE and TABLE.index(nm) > TABLE.index(LD)]
            at_name = later[0] if later else len(order_in)
            want_order = order_in[:at_name] + [LD] + order_in[at_name:]
        else:
            want_order = order_in
        flags["root_order"] = order_out == want_order
        if not rels_add:
            want_rels = zin.read(wrels) if wrels in names else None
        elif wrels in names:
            want_rels = before_end(zin.read(wrels), rels_add)
        else:
            want_rels = package_prefix(zin) + b'<Relationships xmlns="' + RELS.encode() + b'">' + rels_add + b"</Relationships>"
        flags["rels_bytes"] = extra["rels"] == want_rels
        types_in = zin.read("[Content_Types].xml")
        flags["types_bytes"] = extra["types"] == (before_end(types_in, over_add) if over_add else types_in)
        flags["comments_bytes"] = extra["comments"] == want_c
        flags["vml_bytes"] = want_v is not None and extra["vml"] == want_v
        comments_out = authors_out = shapes_out = -1
        rich_out = runs_out = -1
        text_out = 0
        try:
            if extra["comments"] is not None:
                listed, authors = comment_list(extra["comments"])
                comments_out, authors_out = len(listed), len(authors)
                last = listed[-1] if listed else None
                text_out = 1 if last is not None and "".join(last.itertext()) == TEXT.decode() else 0
                flags["comments_read"] = (comments_out == n_comments_in + 1 and last is not None
                                          and last.get("ref") == ref.decode() and last.get("authorId") == str(aid)
                                          and text_out == 1)
                flags["two_runs"] = last is not None and two_runs_ok(last)
                rich_out = sum(1 for c in listed if is_rich(c))
                runs_out = len(rich_runs(last)) if last is not None else -1
                flags["rich_read"] = (rich_out == rich_in + 1 and last is not None and is_rich(last)
                                      and runs_out == 2)
        except ET.ParseError:
            pass
        try:
            if extra["vml"] is not None:
                notes = note_shapes(extra["vml"])
                shapes_out = len(notes)
                last = notes[-1] if notes else None
                rows = [r.text for r in last.iter("{%s}Row" % X)] if last is not None else []
                cols = [c.text for c in last.iter("{%s}Column" % X)] if last is not None else []
                flags["shapes_read"] = (shapes_out == shapes_in + 1 and last is not None
                                        and last.get("id") == "_x0000_s%d" % number
                                        and rows == [str(row)] and cols == [str(col)])
        except ET.ParseError:
            pass
        count_parts = lambda ns: sum(1 for nm in ns if (nm.startswith("xl/comments") and nm.endswith(".xml"))
                                     or (nm.startswith("xl/drawings/vmlDrawing") and nm.endswith(".vml")))
        # The runner's diff for the pair (P1 verification ruling 6): the xml
        # values rows and the descriptor flags against what the rules give.
        xml_rows = -1
        out_only = -1
        want_out_only = sum(values_in(b) for b in appended.values())
        flagged_rows = -1
        want_flagged = -1
        if diff_path is not None:
            rows = [l.split("\t") for l in open(diff_path, encoding="utf-8").read().split("\n") if l]
            values = {c[1]: c for c in rows if len(c) >= 7 and c[0] == "xml" and c[2] == "values"}
            changed = {part} if made_v else set()
            if rels_add and wrels in names:
                changed.add(wrels)
            if over_add:
                changed.add("[Content_Types].xml")
            if got["cin"]:
                changed.add(got["cin"])
            if got["vin"]:
                changed.add(got["vin"])
            xml_want = {nm: values_in(appended[nm]) for nm in changed if nm in appended}
            if e_plant(extra, "xml_values"):
                xml_want = {nm: v + 1 for (nm, v) in xml_want.items()}
            xml_rows = len(values)
            out_only = sum(int(c[6]) for c in values.values())
            flags["xml_values"] = (set(values) == set(xml_want)
                                   and all(values[nm][5] == "0" and values[nm][6] == str(v)
                                           for (nm, v) in xml_want.items()))
            # The entry rows: "entry", the name, the status, ..., the flags in the
            # seventeenth column (the runner's entries.<label>.tsv is these rows
            # behind id, label and row).
            ents = [{"name": c[1], "status": c[2], "flags": c[16]} for c in rows
                    if len(c) == 17 and c[0] == "entry"]
            flagged_rows = sum(1 for r in ents if r["flags"])
            want = {nm: ("descriptor" if bit3(zin, nm) == "1" else "") for nm in changed}
            if e_plant(extra, "flagged"):
                want = {nm: ("" if f else "descriptor") for (nm, f) in want.items()}
            want_flagged = sum(1 for f in want.values() if f)
            flags["flagged"] = (len(ents) > 0 and flagged_rows == want_flagged
                                and all(r["flags"] == want.get(r["name"], "") for r in ents
                                        if r["status"] != "added"))
    
        print(" ".join(
            ["found=1", "planted=%s" % yn(planted),
             "comments_in=%d" % n_comments_in, "comments_out=%d" % comments_out,
             "parts_in=%d" % count_parts(names), "parts_out=%d" % count_parts(out_names),
             "legacy_in=%d" % (0 if made_v else 1), "cpart_in=%d" % (0 if made_c else 1),
             "r_bound_in=%d" % (0 if bound is None else 1),
             "shapes_in=%d" % shapes_in, "shapes_out=%d" % shapes_out,
             "authors_in=%d" % n_authors_in, "authors_out=%d" % authors_out, "authors_want=%d" % authors_want,
             "d=%d" % d, "k=%d" % k, "created=%d" % (int(made_c) + int(made_v)),
             "rich_in=%d" % rich_in, "rich_out=%d" % rich_out, "runs_out=%d" % runs_out,
             "text_out=%d" % text_out, "xml_rows=%d" % xml_rows, "out_only=%d" % out_only,
             "out_only_want=%d" % want_out_only, "flagged_rows=%d" % flagged_rows,
             "flagged_want=%d" % want_flagged,
             "strict=%d" % (1 if strict else 0), "rels_part_in=%d" % (1 if wrels in names else 0)]
            + ["%s=%s" % (f, yn(flags[f])) for f in FLAGS]))
    
    
    main()
